  nodePositions: []
  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What is an Insulin Hexamer?
    basic: "Six insulin monomers form a single hexamer which acts as a storage unit
      for insulin. \nHexamers can assemble and form insulin crystals."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "Insulin and zinc enrichment in the insulin vesicle promotes hexamer
      formation. \nThe hexamer complex has a D3d symmetry which facilitates packing.
      \nHydrophilic residues are arranged outwards, which promotes solubility and
      the formation of a 'water jacket' when packaged. \nThese structural features
      make insulin storage highly efficient in an insulin vesicle. \nThis efficient
      storage is crucial because insulin is secreted in large amounts."
  nodeSpriteLayer: []
